{
  "_about": "Which ingredient words bring which allergens. Used by recipe_eval/allergens.py. Matching is on whole words (plural allowed), case-insensitive. Hand-written and approximate: it errs on the side of flagging (a missed allergen is worse than a false one). It cannot see hidden ingredients (for example lecithin, or oil used in a store-bought sauce) or cross-contact. Covers the 14 EU allergen families (gluten, crustaceans, egg, fish, peanut, soy, milk, tree_nut, celery, mustard, sesame, sulphites, lupin, molluscs); wheat and shellfish are extra convenience tags.",
